Nearly 70% of ICE arrests are of illegal aliens charged or convicted of a crime in the U.S.

WASHINGTON –– U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) announced the arrest of more criminal illegal aliens from across the country, convicted of horrific crimes including child molestation, rape, and sexual battery.

> Yesterday, the brave men and women of ICE arrested more criminal illegal aliens including pedophiles, rapists, and other violent thugs,

said Deputy Assistant Secretary Lauren Bis.

> Criminal illegal aliens who prey on vulnerable children, harm innocent Americans, and commit heinous acts of violence should NEVER be allowed to remain in the U.S. Under President Trump, ICE has removed more than 713,000 illegal aliens from our country, and we now have the lowest murder rate in 125 years.

Yesterday’s arrests include:

